%!PS
% Source of report.pdf, a three-page report with known text for the web report provider tests.
% Rebuild from this folder: gs -q -dNOPAUSE -dBATCH -sDEVICE=pdfwrite -sOutputFile=report.pdf report.ps
/Helvetica findfont 10 scalefont setfont
/L { 72 y moveto show /y y 14 sub def } def

/y 770 def
(Northwind Grid AG Annual Report 2025) L
(Fiscal year from 1 October 2024 to 30 September 2025) L
(This report covers the group and its three segments. It is a test fixture with known) L
(text, written for the web report provider tests of open foresight.) L
(Northwind Grid AG makes switchgear, transformers and grid control software for) L
(distribution system operators in Europe. Revenue rose by six percent to 9.4 billion) L
(euros, and the order backlog reached 21 billion euros at the end of the year.) L
(The board proposes a dividend of 2.10 euros per share. Free cash flow was 1.1 billion) L
(euros. The group employs 41,000 people in 28 countries and runs factories in) L
(Germany, Poland, Spain and India.) L
(The following pages describe the segments and the risks the group sees for the) L
(coming fiscal year, together with the outlook the board gave in November.) L
showpage

/y 770 def
(Smart Infrastructure segment) L
(The segment sells medium voltage switchgear, protection relays and the grid control) L
(software that distribution system operators use to balance demand and local solar) L
(generation. Revenue was 4.8 billion euros and the profit margin was 14.2 percent.) L
(Orders for grid automation software grew by 19 percent, led by utilities in Germany) L
(and the Netherlands that are adding flexible connections for heat pumps and chargers.) L
(The segment opened a relay factory in Wroclaw and doubled its software team in Madrid.) L
(Prices for copper and electrical steel rose during the year, and the segment passed) L
(most of the increase on to customers through price clauses in framework contracts.) L
(Demand for transformers is still higher than the industry can build, and lead times) L
(for large power transformers stayed above two years for most of the fiscal year.) L
showpage

/y 770 def
(Mobility and rail signalling segment) L
(The segment supplies interlockings, train control equipment and maintenance services) L
(to rail operators in Europe and Asia. Revenue was 2.9 billion euros and new orders) L
(reached 3.6 billion euros, so the backlog grew to 11 billion euros. The largest order) L
(of the year was a signalling contract for a regional network in northern Spain.) L
(The segment margin fell to 8.1 percent because two fixed price projects ran over) L
(budget. The board expects the margin to recover in the next fiscal year as these) L
(projects finish and the new digital interlocking platform reaches volume production.) L
(Risks for the coming year include delays in public tenders, the supply of chips for) L
(train control units, and the cost of hiring signalling engineers in Germany.) L
showpage
